                                "example_id": "557a135f-bed9-4796-ab42-768e46ce72a0",
                                "sense_id": "be0ce6aa-57c7-326b-8192-23556336f277",
                                "text": "Rhabdomyoma is the most common of primary cardiac neoplasms found in infants and children. It is rare in adults. Fifty per cent of patients with rhabdomyoma also have tuberous sclerosis—a familial disease consisting of epilepsy, mental retardation, and adenoma sebaceum."
